id: DRAFT-13538-openddl-parser-0.5.2-tag-embedded-version-stale
category: compat, packaging, build-system
build_system: cmake
phase: packaging
match_keywords: static const char *Version, getVersion, PROJECT_VERSION, version string, embedded version, tag version, upstream did not bump, stale version, version mismatch tag
error_signature: "static const char [*]Version[ ]*=[ ]*\"[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\" differs from the official release tag that the archive was fetched from"
error_excerpt: "openddl-parser v0.5.2 tag: code/OpenDDLParser.cpp static const char *Version = \"0.4.0\"; OpenDDLParser::getVersion() returns 0.4.0 while the archive/sha256 pinned by the recipe is the v0.5.2 release. CMakeLists.txt reads PROJECT_VERSION via regex from the same cpp."
root_cause: "The upstream project keeps its version number in a source-level string constant (static const char *Version) exposed through a runtime getVersion() API, but releases new tags without bumping that constant (openddl-parser v0.5.2 still contains 0.4.0). CMake projects that regex-parse the version from this cpp then carry the stale number into build metadata and any generated versioned artifacts."
rec_approach: "1) Treat the official release tag as the authoritative version for the recipe/archive (conandata url+sha256 pinned to the tag tarball, conanfile version = tag). 2) Do NOT patch the embedded version string - it is an upstream fact; state it in notes.md and the PR body instead of forcing a diff against the official tag. 3) If the project uses PROJECT_VERSION to generate file names or header macros, explicitly override with the tag version in generate(); if it only affects an informational runtime API (getVersion), no override is needed. 4) Consumer/test asserts must not hard-assert the version string equals the tag version - assert the API is callable and non-empty, so an upstream versioning fact never reads as an adaptation failure."
solution: "openddl-parser 0.5.2: kept recipe version 0.5.2 (official tag, sha256 8058caacdc989a010c2ad3ab62df99f9f3034b4981649c5fb832efa6fbf10c36), no source patch; consumers call OpenDDLParser::getVersion() without asserting equality. conan-verify ohos-aarch64 passed: upstream gtest 125/125, test_package + consumer + test_ohos (ELF64 AArch64/musl/no host-path leak/real parse) all passed."
fallback: "If a downstream consumer truly needs the corrected string, a versioned patch bumping only the constant deltas the package against the official tag and must be explained in the PR; avoid unless a runtime feature depends on the value."
prescan_pattern: "static const char [*]Version[ ]*=[ ]*\"[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\\.[0-9]+\""
verify_builds: "local conan create ohos-aarch64 (openddl-parser 0.5.2): upstream suite 125/125 PASSED, test_package CTest passed, consumer_openddl_parser OK, test_ohos OHOS_SPECIAL_PASS"
severity: 2
status: draft
last_updated: 2026-09-29
similar_to: DRAFT-8425-libusbsio-2.1.13-upstream-deleted-equivalent-source